# OpenGamepadUI — the gamepad shell gamescope hosts. Precompiled aarch64 release pin.
#
# Auto-discovered by rootfs/customize-base.sh like every packages/*/prebuilt.pin: fetched,
# sha256-verified on the host, and extracted into the release base.
#
# Upstream publishes a distro-agnostic aarch64 tarball (Godot export + the Rust GDExtension core +
# the reaper), so nothing is compiled here. The archive is rooted at opengamepadui/ and carries a
# Makefile and a .gdignore BESIDE usr/, so it unpacks with strip 2 into /usr: everything under
# opengamepadui/usr/ lands at /usr/..., and the two top-level files (two path components) are
# dropped by tar instead of landing at the target's /.
#
# deps: libxinerama. Godot's X11 display server dlopen()s libXinerama and refuses to start without
# it; nothing else in the base pulls it in. OGUI must run as an X11 client: it drives gamescope
# through the X atoms on gamescope's nested Xwayland (GAMESCOPECTRL_BASELAYER_APPID,
# GAMESCOPE_FOCUSABLE_APPS, STEAM_OVERLAY, ...). Every other library it loads (X11, Vulkan, EGL,
# ALSA/Pulse, fontconfig, D-Bus, udev, wayland) is already in the base. libspeechd (text-to-speech)
# is optional and deliberately absent.
#
# OGUI's SELF-UPDATER is removed from the image (rootfs/conf/trim.list): on a read-only RAUC root
# the OS image is what carries the OGUI version.
#
# To bump: pick a tag at https://github.com/ShadowBlip/OpenGamepadUI/releases and set
# version + url + sha256 together (sha256 from the asset's .sha256.txt sidecar).

name: opengamepadui
version: 0.46.1
url: https://github.com/ShadowBlip/OpenGamepadUI/releases/download/v0.46.1/opengamepadui-aarch64.tar.gz
sha256: 84b075f8f8c3925b9e0925705adab37f9237a8ff6eeabc6cf4c3af927520413c
strip: 2
dest: /usr

deps: libxinerama
